WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.520
Discover...

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.740
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.810
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.150
Wow...

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:30.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.530
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:46.250
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.930
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.470
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:56.880
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.430
Discover...

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.240
Night sky

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.110
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.580
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:21.160
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.450
Wow...

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.990
#05 The Sudden Visitor

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.280
Tenn Tenn, what's up? You need something?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.310
Don't just give me terrible nicknames.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.790
Here. A gift for you.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.520
Hell yeah! This is King Pudding!

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.830
Tenn Tenn, can I eat all of this?

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.140
Do whatever you want.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.210
Thanks, Tenn Tenn!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.210
I told you...

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.760
Where's Riku's room?

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.210
Second from the right.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.120
Two, four, six, eight...

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.120
I see.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.460
All right! There's ten of them!

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.960
Even if I only eat one per hour,
 that's ten hours' worth!

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.940
Yotsuba-san, what are you shouting about?

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.620
Snacks again? You eat too many of those.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.940
They were a gift!

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:22.640
From who?

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.730
Tenn Tenn.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:27.220
Tenn Tenn? Have you adopted a cat?

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.580
You know Nanase-san is allergic to pet hair.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.340
By the way, how large is it?

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:37.340
How large? Um... On the small side?

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.500
What? It's a kitten? What color?

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.720
Whitish?

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.380
A white kitten? How cu—

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.730
No, for Nanase-san's sake, we should 
catch it immediately and deal with it.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.960
I am my usual self; what of it?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.410
Huh? You're looking for a kitten?

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.130
You're the one who brought it up!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.250
Your pudding can wait until 
after we've found it.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.110
What?

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.080
Hold this dish.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.990
And this milk.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.240
Now, let's go find it.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.250
What? Man, this sucks...

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.500
<i>Everyone, thank you for today!</i>

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.380
Tenn-nii is always so cool.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.010
<i>Thank you! I love you!</i>

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.440
Liar. He was angry and scowling.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.650
Yes? I'm not hungry yet.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.580
I said, I'm not—

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.970
Tenn-nii?!

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.110
A dream...

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.610
It's not a dream.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.400
I fell asleep while watching—

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.790
You're not asleep.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:46.900
It's really you?

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:48.790
That's right.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:57.000
Good for you. You're keeping your room clean.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.930
How are you feeling? 
Have you been seeing the doctor?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.570
Y-Yeah...

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.410
Are you sleeping well?

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.520
You need to rest and keep your throat warm.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.810
Okay...

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.880
You were watching a TRIGGER concert?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.470
Ah, yeah.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.630
I'm gonna turn this off, okay?

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.990
I'm here now. You'll keep 
me company, won't you?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.400
Yeah!

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.750
Oh. What a worthwhile way to spend our time.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:35.680
I have successfully converted you.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.000
I've seen that anime a bunch of times before.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.760
Huh? There's no one here.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.690
There's stew and King Pudding.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.260
Is this Tamaki's?

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.640
<i>Hello! Re:vale here!</i>

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.390
Re:vale... is here?!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.390
Oh?!

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.370
This place is nice and big.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.120
Wh-What brings you here today?

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:06.230
Your leader is blocking my calls, 
so I came to express my regrets.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.290
Is he around?

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.330
I'm here on a special mission to find Nagi.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.680
Aha, found him!

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.680
Now world peace can be preserved!

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.910
Oh! A special mission!

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.560
How exciting!

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.960
Nagi-kun, you accepted that awfully quickly!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.190
Um, Yamato-san is out right now.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.340
We'll wait in your room, then.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.050
What?!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.090
It's King Pudding!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.090
Can I have some?

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.140
Smells good. We hadn't eaten dinner yet.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.960
Actually, um...

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.060
We're Re:vale, so...

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.650
We're your seniors, right?

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:43.150
M-Make yourselves at home. 
Have something to eat.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.310
Want something to drink? How about to eat?

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.150
I'm fine.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.400
I see. Um...

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.070
There were a bunch of things I wanted to
 talk about, but I forgot all of them.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.340
Then, how about I start?

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.170
Okay.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.340
Riku, is there someone you like?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.360
What?! N-No.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.420
There is a girl I'm sort of
 interested in, though...

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.930
Would you be sad if you 
couldn't see her very often?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.060
I think I'd be really sad.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:19.440
And what if you arranged to finally see her 
again, but she couldn't make it anymore?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.570
I'd be sad, and probably worried.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.890
Tenn-nii, is there someone you like?

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.160
Are you asking for relationship advice?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.200
What do you think? Take a guess.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.340
I'm not sure. You've always been popular.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.210
What's she like? Does she 
live somewhere far away?

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.580
My lover is my fans.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.630
I never do anything to sadden my fans.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.570
I never break promises I make to my fans.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.840
It's only natural for an idol.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.850
Promises?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.970
Concert tickets.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.600
They're a promise that 
you'll be there on that day

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.860
to do your best for your fans 
with a smile on your face.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:04.100
You can't keep promises.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.480
You haven't until now,
and you can't going forward.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:13.540
I told Tamaki to leave some!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.470
Man, I'm hungry.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.510
All right, sir. We've arrived.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.770
You guys reek of alcohol!

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.010
Here! Could you carry him?

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.640
What? Who is this guy?

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.180
Don't bring strangers into our 
home when there are minors—

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:32.930
Haisai!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:32.930
(Hey!)

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.850
This is Tsunashi Ryunosuke!

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.850
Why'd you bring this home?!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.420
It's not like that.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.200
I went drinking with him because 
we made plans the other day.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.860
Then this guy wouldn't stop throwing 'em back.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.890
I have no idea what he's saying.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.800
Anshi? Mishi kawattagaya?

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.800
(Huh? Did we go somewhere else?)

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.500
Kuma karaoke yaibishiga?

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.500
(Is this a karaoke place?)

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.830
You're right. I have no 
idea what he's saying.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.210
Chaya utaundo!

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.210
(All right, let's sing!)

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.700
Yasa shime kai bannai hiya sasayassa!

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.700
(You gotta round the night off with a bang!)

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:54.700
Right?

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.030
Maiku to rimokon kai naiba?

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.030
(Where are the mics and remotes?)

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.970
Anshe, Mitsuki-kun mensore.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.970
(Mitsuki-kun, you came, too?)

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:03.100
Eh, uttu ya arangutou nini yatta aruyashiya?

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:03.100
(I thought you were the younger brother, 
but is it true that you're older?)

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.480
Wan mo nini yashiga. Chakushi.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.480
(I'm an older brother, too. The eldest.)

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.760
Oriko gwa yone uttu.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.760
(Younger brothers are so cute.)

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.310
Watta mo chore no tame ni hamaranneya.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.310
(We've both got to work hard to 
support our younger brothers.)

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.800
Yassai! Ey, ey!

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.800
(Come on! Let's go!)

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.050
Huh? What?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.640
Uh... mensore.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.640
(Uh... Welcome.)

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.020
Mensore!

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.890
He's been like this.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.230
You've been conversing with 
him using just "mensore"?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.980
That doesn't work for everything!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.230
Anshe, unju na utan kai utasundo!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.230
(All right, let's sing one of your songs!)

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.480
Shaking your heart!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.410
Whoa, he started singing!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.940
Shaking your beat!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.590
Icha ribachore!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.590
(Come on, together now!)

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:38.840
Racing through time!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.080
Maybe I'll have something to drink, too.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.860
Shall we resume drinking, then?

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.330
Eh? Nuyaga?

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.330
(Eh? What?)

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.250
Mensore!

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:45.240
Mensore!

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.130
I can't keep promises?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:53.480
The worst thing an idol can do
 is disappoint their fans.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:58.760
I'd never allow someone to get hurt 
because they're a Kujo Tenn fan.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.550
I don't want them to regret being my fan.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.110
Even if they stop being a fan someday,

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.270
I want them to smile when they look 
back on the time they spent on me.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.210
You're a good, hardworking boy.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:20.240
That's why I forgot about the younger brother 
who couldn't run and recognized you as a rival.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:26.620
But I realized something at your concert 
and our rehearsal the other day.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.040
At this rate, you'll only make 
yourself and your fans unhappy.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.660
That's not—

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:33.960
There's no substitute for our work.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.920
And if there is, it proves you're second-rate.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.220
The harder you try to be first-rate,

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.200
the more trouble you'll cause for 
the support structures around you.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:51.530
We stand onstage entrusted with 
the lives of countless people.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.130
For the four and a half 
minutes you spend singing,

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:58.640
there are people who worked for four 
months and studied for four years.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:04.200
One of us making a mistake can 
ruin their efforts in an instant.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.540
Do you realize that?

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:10.060
I... I just want to sing with everyone.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:14.040
If you just want to sing with your 
friends, go to karaoke with them.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.550
Even I'd be willing to applaud for you there.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.960
Didn't you say you wanted 
to know why I left home?

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.310
I'll tell you.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.520
It's because Dad's club forgot their 
responsibility to entertain their customers.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.480
What?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.610
Why do you think the club closed down?

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:36.460
Because Kujo arrived and put pressure on them
 when they were having money problems.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:41.740
Wrong. It's because the club's economic 
struggles were impacting the dancers.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.740
They danced anxiously with sullen smiles.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.750
They forced themselves to sing 
through their distraction.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.410
Who would pay money to see that kind of show?

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.130
At first I rebelled against Kujo-san, too.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:11:01.010
But when he showed me the world of 
professionals, my eyes were opened.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:05.570
Even when meteors are falling 
and the world is in despair,

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:08.060
it's our job to smile and sing.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.980
Kujo-san taught me that.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.380
That's why I've followed him.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.070
I'll say it again.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.960
You cannot do this job.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.940
You should quit being an idol.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.500
Tenn Tenn!

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.440
Tenn Tenn-chan!

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.290
He's not on the third floor, either.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.070
There's no one living here yet.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.380
We have no choice.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:46.050
I definitely only brought this 
so we could lure out Tenn Tenn.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.330
Surely, a curious kitten won't 
be able to resist this sound.

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:50.710
Iorin, you're kind of close...

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.000
What a relief I <i>just happened </i>
to have it in my room.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.310
Tenn Tenn's in Rikkun's room.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:55.910
What?

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.040
He's in Nanase-san's room?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.350
Pet hair isn't good for him.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.660
He's only got hair on his head.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.670
Only his head?!

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.510
Oh, and his eyebrows.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.040
<b>Eyebrows</b>

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.040
What?

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:12.550
Perhaps he ran away after 
his owner shaved his hair.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.820
Poor thing.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.790
If the cat's in Nanase-san's room, 
we'll have to go get him.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.420
There's a cat in Rikkun's room?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.490
Isn't that what you said?!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:22.760
I didn't say that.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:26.430
He's not there? Then we'll look elsewhere.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:31.260
Tenn Tenn, we have milk!

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:31.260
Man, this is too much work.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:32.970
Tenn Tenn!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.140
Meow! Kitty, where are you?

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.150
I may resort to using the Usamimi Friend.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:42.250
I end up being hard on Tamaki-kun 
because I want him to act responsibly.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:43.150
I see, I see.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:47.290
Apparently someone told Tamaki-kun 
it was okay for him to be rude.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.410
Don't worry. I'm on your side.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:54.020
Nagi, can you autograph this one, too?

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.810
This one's for Kaoru-chan.

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:59.250
Oh. This doesn't seem like 
a special mission at all.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.100
It's very ordinary.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:02.660
That's not true.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:06.830
This signed merchandise will 
cause the event of the century.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:07.590
Why?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.910
It's still a secret!

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.810
Maybe we should include kiss marks, too.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.770
Here, lipstick. Purse your lips.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.770
Oh...

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:18.520
Kissing photographs of yourself? 
How very perverted of you.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.020
Let's go Wake me up!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:25.220
Let's dream together!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.660
Oh, man! So cool! So sexy!

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:29.280
Twilight for the two of us!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.280
He's dead drunk but he's singing for real.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.860
Yasaru sokutuyo?

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.860
(You guys hungry?)

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:35.460
Tansui kabutsu gwa toritai anni.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:35.460
(I want something carbonated.)

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.460
Yeah, I know what you mean. Yeah, yeah.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.210
What'd he say?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.810
I think he said he was hungry.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.420
Come to think of it, I haven't 
had dinner yet, either.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.550
Should we order soba?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.220
Sounds good. Tsunashi-san, 
you want some soba?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.140
Kamushiru, kamushiru!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.140
(I sure do!)

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.520
Quit being an idol?

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.320
That's right. Meeting expectations. 
Keeping promises.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.630
There's a lot of that kind 
of pressure in this world.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.360
It's a hard world for you, so...

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:08.870
Did you go with Kujo because 
our parents were wrong?

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.910
So you <i>did</i> abandon us.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.330
Riku...

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:18.220
If you thought they were wrong, 
you should've said so.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:20.630
You could've helped us!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.600
The club was gone, and so were you...

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.640
Mom was always crying about it.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.510
I even saw Dad crying when he was alone.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.060
I was always crying, too.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:34.920
I thought you hated having to take
care of me pushed onto you.

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:37.590
Riku, it's not like that. I—

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:38.180
Don't touch me!

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:43.360
You abandoned our family when 
things were hardest for us!

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:48.810
Just because you thought Kujo, who drove 
the club out of business, was right!

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:52.010
Riku, don't get too excited. 
Calm down and list—

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:52.990
It's not fair!

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:57.440
You abandoned your family to become 
an idol, but you're telling me to quit.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:03.750
I... I always thought that once 
I grew up and became stronger

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:07.760
that you'd ask me to sing with you.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:15.370
But you never needed me.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.520
Riku, that's not true.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.780
I never forgot about you, even onc—

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.390
Tenn Tenn-chan.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.360
We have milk for you.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:28.520
We've been together ever
since we were born. So...

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:32.820
Taste you taste you! Show me more!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:30.930
Hey, you're bothering everyone!

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.820
Bring the volume down, buddy.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.270
Toire mayaga?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.270
(Where's the bathroom?)

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.230
Tenn Tenn-chan. Tenn Tenn-chan.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.810
What I'm trying to say is...

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.980
Meow. Kitty, where are you?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.980
Yamamura Soba here.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.620
Shut up!

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:46.750
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.110
Thanks for coming.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.340
Oh, the guy who looks just like Yaotome.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.830
I get that all the time.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.720
Here. Three orders of 
tempura soba. They're hot.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.180
Oh, thanks.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.890
Good evening. I made you guys something.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:01.390
Hey, Manager.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.980
Hey, it's been a while.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.920
Good to see you again, Mr. Soba Deliveryman.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.980
You cooked something?

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.690
Yes. There's chikuzen-ni and 
all sorts of other things.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:11.440
I'm not sure that they'll like it, though.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.980
Really? If they don't want it, I'll eat it.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.320
Do you want me to carry
that to the table for you?

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.930
What? Oh, thank you.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.170
Excuse the intrusion.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.660
Huh? What?

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.710
That should do it.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:28.380
Wow, it looks so different.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.870
Impressive as always, Mr. Soba Deliveryman.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:30.550
Right?

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:35.970
Hey, no soba deliveryman should 
ever be that handsome.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:41.100
<b>Yamamura Soba</b>

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.440
Hasn't Tsunashi-san been 
in the bathroom a while?

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:41.100
Well, he did have a lot to drink.

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:45.710
You really do always look just like Gaku-san.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:49.020
Really? What's this Yaotome guy like?

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:54.950
He seems scary, but he's kind like you.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.980
Do you like Yaotome Gaku?

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.760
Yes, very much!

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.160
I think a girl like you might be able
 to make Yaotome fall for her.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.800
I could n-never!

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.750
Besides, Gaku-san is everyone's idol.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.790
I could absolutely <i>never</i> form a special 
relationship with the talent.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:14.490
<i>Never... never... absolutely never...</i>

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.970
It's the least you can expect from someone 
working at an entertainment agency.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.800
I know my place.

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:23.760
I see...

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.020
Mr. Soba Deliveryman?

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:27.970
How about a humble soba deliveryman, then?

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:28.400
What?

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.660
When are you free? I'll make time for you.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.570
I'll take you anywhere you want to go.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.340
You won't be bored.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:39.840
This humble soba deliveryman promises 
you the best day you've ever had.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:41.570
Don't you want to spend that with me?

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:43.580
You will, right?

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:48.360
Um, I appreciate the thought, 
but I don't do that kind of thing

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:51.920
with people I don't know very well...

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.180
Of course not.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:55.340
Pathetic...

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:56.600
You!

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:57.320
Kujo-san?!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.830
Kujo Tenn?!

00:17:58.830 --> 00:17:59.720
Why are you here?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.220
Shut up. Be quiet.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:03.470
What? Why are you mad?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:04.940
Not only were you rejected,

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.350
but you hit on her while pretending to 
be someone else and got rejected <i>again</i>.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.520
Pathetic.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.330
What are you talking about?

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.070
Are you sure you don't have the wrong person?

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.400
Hey, aren't you supposed to 
be the sexiest man alive?

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.720
Oh, no! This is our local soba deliveryman.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:20.870
Right, Yamamura-san?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.020
Yeah, I guess...

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.590
Tenn Tenn.

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:26.260
Kitty.

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:27.710
Are they practicing for a skit?

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:28.730
TRIGGER?!

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:31.280
Don't, Iori! Don't get involved! Stay away!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.830
He'll get mad.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:33.620
What?

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.760
Iorin, it's an emergency!

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.300
My King Pudding is gone!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:40.870
That's all?

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.070
Don't give me that!

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:46.180
Why did I bother wandering 
around calling for some kitty?!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.450
For Tenn Tenn!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.200
I'm having an important 
conversation. Could you be quiet?

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.980
Also, stop calling me Tenn Tenn.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.940
What? How old are you?

00:18:54.940 --> 00:19:00.190
I can't believe you thought a nickname 
as cute as "Tenn Tenn" could refer to—

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.280
Tenn Tenn, my pudding's gone!

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.080
<b>Tenn Tenn = Tenn</b>

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.080
You mean, <i>he's</i> Tenn Tenn?!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.400
So, where is my apology?

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.470
Hey, what's going on here?

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:11.060
Is this a prank?

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.000
Osaka Sogo 
Incoming Call...

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:14.000
So's calling.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:15.460
Hello?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.840
What? <i>He's</i> here?

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.140
Oh, I'm at Shinbashi.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.090
I'll probably be back in the morning.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:25.280
Boss, another one!

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:26.630
Huh? What?

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:27.470
Sure thing!

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.960
Thanks!

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:31.940
Also, don't believe anything he says.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.010
I'm on your side.

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:38.020
If he says that, it means he's trying 
to use mimicry to prey on you.

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:38.840
Yeah.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:43.000
King...? Oh, right.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.480
But there were ten!

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.030
Got it.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.740
Later.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.220
What did Sogo say?

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.670
So and Re:vale are in Nagi's room.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:50.980
Re:vale?!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.020
I'm going to say hello—

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:54.650
Don't, don't!

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:55.540
Why not?

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:58.310
Apparently Re:vale ate the King Puddings.

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:00.720
I'm gonna murder whoever ate them!

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:02.140
See?

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:06.220
Y-You're right. I couldn't allow 
something to happen to them.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:08.100
Riku!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:08.770
Riku-san?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:17.400
No matter what you say... 
I'll never quit IDOLiSH7!

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.650
Quit IDOLiSH7?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:25.620
You may have abandoned me, 
but the others need me!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:30.110
Iori, didn't you say you'd 
make me a superstar?

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:30.790
What?

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:34.940
Really? Iori, you're capable of 
making such passionate remarks?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.300
Ah, to be young.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:39.700
I-It's not like that! I never said
 anything so embarrassing.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.400
You did! Tell Tenn-nii!

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:46.770
I only said that in the heat of the moment—

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:47.590
Say it!

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:55.690
N-Nanase-san, I promise I'll 
make you a superstar...

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.670
So young!

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.570
Shut up, you drunks!

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.300
And Manager, didn't you tell me?

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.570
You said I was essential to IDOLiSH7!

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.660
Yes, I did say that.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.870
Tell that to Tenn-nii!

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:08.420
What?

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:13.290
R-Riku-san is essential and 
important to IDOLiSH7!

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:14.750
He can't quit!

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.990
See? You're the only one who's mean to me!

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.080
You're just...

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:21.780
Riku-san, are you all right?

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:24.360
Riku, listen.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.220
I won't!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.510
You won't hear me out?

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:28.720
Never!

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.550
I see. Forget it, then.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:37.680
I'll never recognize you as an idol.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:42.280
Hey, I don't know what happened, 
but why don't we all just—

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.400
Shut up, deliveryman!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.010
You...

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:49.350
Sorry, sorry. I fell asleep in the bathroom.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.160
I'm all sobered up now though—

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.160
What's everyone doing here?!

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:55.690
This isn't the karaoke place?

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:57.100
We're leaving, Ryu.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:21:59.210
Did something happen?

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:00.710
Nothing.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:04.000
Just leave your dishes
outside when you're done.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.220
Thanks for coming.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:18.830
I hate you... Tenn-nii.

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Voice"</b>
